  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\n\nHigh pressure will be in place over the region through the\nweekend into early next week. The high pressure will weaken a\ncold front as it attempts to push through the region Thursday\ninto Friday. This should act as a slight cooling trend. With \nthe dry pattern continuing lows should end up slightly below \nmodel guidance with highs ending up a bit warmer most days. \nAnother weak cold front looks to push into the region around \nTuesday next week. Some ensemble members have a few showers with\nit. For now, signal too low to mention any shower chances.",
